cular block episode. This represents a serious potential patient-safety risk (severity 3) due to the failure or missed detection in a safety-critical function that might have led to serious harm, even if no harm actually occurred in the reported event. While the telemetry log and emergency response record disagree on the onset time, this discrepancy does not change the outcome; however, it highlights potential issues with data integrity and synchronization which requires investigation. The device incorporates electronic programmable systems (software), requiring adherence to principles of development lifecycle, risk management, verification, and validation as outlined in EU MDR Annex I, Section 17.2. Furthermore, manufacturers must ensure repeatability, reliability, and performance in line with intended use, and adopt appropriate means to eliminate or reduce risks in the event of a single fault condition (EU MDR Annex I, Section 17.1). The incident also implicates design controls as the device is automated with computer software (21 CFR \u00a7 820.10(c)).", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 3}, "final_report_sha256": "0ecae231ab3a6f6831194a8b774044e0fe295a72afa09cd7b620d43b9e4972e2", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 1, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["clinical_shacl_nonconformance_routes_review"], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0037", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 1, "run_id": "inloop_SYN-IND-0037_b710ede5", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0037", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 3, "shacl_findings": [{"message": "Predicted severity 3 is below derived clinical floor 4. For the five curated scenarios the derived severity floor equals the labelled ground-truth severity; treat this as a one-sided under-call screen, not an independent correctness oracle.", "severity": "Violation", "shape": "concept_severity_undercall"}, {"me